  "question": {
    "text": "The time period of a spring-mass system is <math><mi>T</mi></math>. If this spring is cut into two parts, whose lengths are in the ratio&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>2</mn></math>, and the same mass is attached to the longer part, the new time period will be",
    "image": null
  },
